# V2-I High Contrast (prompt 019 §4, FUT-47): `ui hc-on` simulates Windows High Contrast with the
# system colours of "High Contrast Black" / "High Contrast White" (live WM_SETTINGCHANGE uses the
# same path with GetSysColor). System colours only: no scheme tint, no custom colours.
command mode light
command scheme glacier
wait-idle
assert hc == 0
ui hc-on black
wait-idle
assert hc == 1
assert dark == 1
assert pal.bg == #000000
assert pal.text == #ffffff
assert pal.link == #ffff00
assert pal.accent == #1aebff
assert pal.code_bg == #000000
snapshot hc-black.png
# The settings panel and its focus ring (COLOR_HIGHLIGHT, visible without keyboard use).
ui click settings
wait-idle
assert settings == open
snapshot hc-black-settings.png
# Settings font enumeration (DirectWrite system collection) under ACG (prompt 019 §4, ADR-0001).
ui settings-click typography.body_font
wait-idle
assert font_list > 5
ui settings-close
wait-idle
assert settings == closed
ui hc-on white
wait-idle
assert dark == 0
assert pal.bg == #ffffff
assert pal.text == #000000
assert pal.link == #00009f
assert pal.accent == #37006e
ui hc-off
wait-idle
assert hc == 0
assert pal.bg != #000000
command scheme default
command mode system
wait-idle
